= La cartera

The offer arrives with the discretion of large sums: a cartera — a real one. A subsecretaría in the agrarian reform, or the directorate of a paraestatal nobody audits, for one of the Movement's serious names. The emissary is at pains to note what this is not: not a bribe, not a charola, nothing so vulgar. It is the system doing what the system does with talent it cannot shoot and has tired of watching — hiring it.

And it is, everyone in the leadership understands, a genuine fork: the post carries real budget, real signatures, real capacity to move real land to real campesinos. It also carries the sexenio's leash, the informe's applause, and a photograph beside the President that no explanation will ever fully caption.

- @aceptar_cartera: Take the post. Budget is power; power is the point. The photograph is the price.
- @negociar_cartera: Neither accept nor refuse: trade the offer for placements lower down — twenty desks instead of one chair.
- @rechazar_cartera: Refuse, publicly enough to be heard. The Movement is not staffing the state; it is replacing it.

@aceptar_cartera
on-arrival: funds += 8; political_capital += 4; sup_peasants += 3; absorcion += 12; sup_students -= 4; fac_nueva_izquierda -= 4; unity -= 3

The compañero takes office and is, precisely as feared, good at it: ejido titles move that stalled for decades, a irrigation budget lands where the maps said it never would. The campo notices. So does everyone else: the informe cites the appointment as proof of the system's breadth, the photograph runs every anniversary, and in the assemblies the young militants begin using the compañero's name in the past tense. The stomach never argues. It just keeps the guest for dinner.

- @post_event: Continuar.

@negociar_cartera
choose-if: political_capital >= 6
unavailable-subtitle: Counter-offers require standing the antechambers respect — more capital than you hold.
on-arrival: political_capital -= 3; absorcion += 5; inteligencia += 4; funds += 3; pri_reformist_rel += 2

The counter-offer amuses the emissary, which is the sound of it working: instead of one chair with a photograph, twenty desks without one — analysts, field inspectors, a records clerk in exactly the right basement. The system grants it, half as a courtesy, half as flypaper. Twenty of yours are inside now, useful in twenty quiet ways, and every one of them is also a hostage to comfort. The reformist road in one transaction: leverage and leash, purchased together, non-separable.

- @post_event: Continuar.

@rechazar_cartera
on-arrival: absorcion -= 8; unity += 3; sup_students += 2; pri_reformist_rel -= 5; funds -= 2

The refusal is delivered in a letter the Movement publishes before the system can pretend it was never offered — a small discourtesy that costs real relationships in the antechambers and buys something the antechambers cannot price: the base's renewed certainty about what the Movement is for. The emissary's superiors note, with professional irritation, that this left still prefers being feared to being fed. The file annotation is almost admiring: *no está en venta todavía.* Not for sale. Yet.

- @post_event: Continuar.

@el_abrazo
title: El abrazo
new-page: true
subtitle: The stomach finishes its work
face-image: img/charola.jpg
tags: event
view-if: via = "institucional" and absorcion >= 70 and abrazo_done = 0
priority: 4
max-visits: 1
on-arrival: abrazo_done = 1

= El abrazo

It arrives without a meeting, because it no longer needs one: the realization, assembling itself across a season of small facts, that the Movement has become *manageable* — and that the system knows it. The invitations arrive before the requests now. The posts renew themselves. The confrontations are scheduled, like maintenance. Somewhere in the last few years the antechambers stopped being enemy territory and became, in the file's own serene annotation, *interlocutores responsables.*

This is the embrace. It is warm, it is generous, and it is how the system has ended every opposition it could not shoot: not with a betrayal but with a thousand reasonable accommodations, each one defensible, the sum of which is a tame left that delivers its sector on schedule — a PPS with better martyrs.

There is still time to be something else. Barely, and at a price.

- @romper_abrazo: Break it. Walk out of the antechambers loudly — back to the political road, the plazas, the enemy's honest hatred.
- @aceptar_abrazo: Stay. Inside is where the budgets are; history can be moved in millimeters; someone must be at the table.

@romper_abrazo
choose-if: unity >= 40
unavailable-subtitle: Walking out takes a party united enough to survive the funcionarios' resignations — yours is not.
on-arrival: {!
Q.via = "politica";
Q.absorcion = 25;
Q.pri_reformist_rel -= 15;
Q.funds -= 5;
Q.sup_students += 4;
Q.sup_workers += 2;
Q.unity -= 4;
Q.political_capital += 3;
Q.fe_voto += 2;
!}

The rupture is performed in public, because only public things are irreversible: the posts resigned in one coordinated week, the letter read from the tribune naming exactly what was offered and what it cost, the antechambers' hospitality returned unconsumed. A third of the placed cadres refuse to come out — the stomach keeps what it has digested — and the relationships of a decade close like doors down a corridor. What walks out is smaller, poorer, and unmistakably alive. In the colonias they say it plainly: *volvieron.* They came back.

- @post_event: Continuar.

@aceptar_abrazo
on-arrival: absorcion = 85; funds += 6; political_capital += 3; sup_students -= 6; sup_workers -= 3; fe_voto -= 3; guerrilla_meter += 3; fac_nueva_izquierda -= 6

The decision is never announced because it was never exactly made: the Movement simply continues, inside, reasonable, funded, consulted — and the country files it accordingly. The young go elsewhere: to the coordinadoras, to the new little parties, some to the mountains, taking with them the future's energy and leaving the apparatus's calm. The system has added one more instrument to its orchestra. It plays, from now on, mostly on schedule.

- @post_event: Continuar.

@la_primera_curul
title: La primera curul
new-page: true
subtitle: The tribune the regime cannot switch off
face-image: img/congreso.jpg
tags: event
view-if: via = "institucional" and izq_seats >= 1 and curul_seen = 0
priority: 4
max-visits: 1
on-arrival: curul_seen = 1

= La primera curul

The credential is a laminated absurdity — *Diputado Federal* over a name that spent thirty years in the government's other files — and walking onto the floor of the Chamber with it is the strangest sensation in the Party's history: the enemy's own house, entered through the front door, by invitation, on the record. The curules smell of furniture polish and impunity. The PRI benches regard you the way a body regards a splinter: without alarm, with intent to expel by natural process.

And there it is, the thing the whole reformist wager was placed on: the tribune. A microphone the regime cannot switch off, in a chamber the press must report, minutes that enter the Republic's permanent record. Fifty years of the Party's dead have no monument. You have, now, four minutes of recognized time and a stenographer obliged to write down whatever you say. The maiden speech is being drafted six ways in six caucus rooms.

- @curul_incendiaria: Read the names. Spend the maiden speech on the disappeared, into the record, at full volume — let them expel you shouting.
- @curul_quirurgica: Be surgical. A precise, unanswerable indictment on one concrete outrage — win the argument, not the ejection.
- @curul_programa: Lay out the program. Use the platform to speak past the chamber to the country — what the left is *for*, not only against.

@curul_incendiaria
on-arrival: sup_students += 4; memorial += 1; legitimidad_regimen -= 3; expediente += 3; pri_reformist_rel -= 4; absorcion -= 4; unity += 2

You read the list. Not all of it — they cut the microphone at minute three — but enough of it entered the Diario de los Debates that the names are now, permanently, a state document: the Republic's own printing office has published its dead over the Party's signature. The PRI benches call you to order; the gavel falls; the galleries do not stay silent. It changes no vote and cannot be unprinted, and of those two facts the second is the one the base carries home. The reformist road just proved it still has teeth — the antechambers noticed the tooth marks.

- @post_event: Continuar.

@curul_quirurgica
on-arrival: political_capital += 4; sup_middle += 3; legitimidad_regimen -= 2; fe_voto += 2; pri_reformist_rel += 1

You pick one outrage — a specific fraud, a specific torture, a specific budget line that fed a specific general — and you build it like a lawyer, dates and documents, no adjective the record can dismiss as rhetoric. The PRI has no answer because there is no answer, only a change of subject, and the change of subject is itself reported. It is the reformist road at its best: not the plaza's roar but the scalpel's precision, the argument won so cleanly that even the middle class that fears the left finds itself, uncomfortably, nodding.

- @post_event: Continuar.

@curul_programa
on-arrival: sup_students += 2; sup_middle += 2; ax_electoral += 3; fe_voto += 3; pri_reformist_rel += 2; absorcion += 2

You decline both the martyr's roar and the prosecutor's knife and do the rarer thing: you describe the country the left would build, concretely, as if it were possible — because from a recognized tribune, for the first time, saying so is not a fantasy but a legislative position. It reaches past the benches to the living rooms; some who had written the left off as pure grievance hear, unexpectedly, a governing imagination. It also, faintly, warms you toward the chamber's own logic — the seduction of speaking as if you already half-belonged.

- @post_event: Continuar.

@la_comision
title: La comisión
new-page: true
subtitle: The tedious work where the real power hides
face-image: img/cards/pleno.jpg
tags: event
view-if: via = "institucional" and izq_seats >= 1 and year >= 1980 and time >= comision_last + 20
priority: 2
frequency: 55
max-visits: 3
on-arrival: comision_last = time

= La comisión

The glamour of the tribune is one percent of the job; the other ninety-nine is the committees, where the Republic is actually written, in rooms with no press and worse coffee. A seat has opened on one that matters — Presupuesto, or Reforma Agraria, or Gobernación itself — and it is offered to your caucus, because the reform's arithmetic needs the opposition to be *seen* doing the boring work that legitimizes the whole apparatus.

It is a genuine dilemma dressed as a scheduling question. The committee is real leverage — amendments, the budget line moved a millimeter, the inspector's report that cannot be buried once it is minuted. It is also a time sink that domesticates: a deputy deep in subsection drafting is a deputy who has not been to a plaza in a year, and the base can tell.

- @comision_trabajar: Do the work. Put your most serious cadre on it and move the country in millimeters no one applauds.
- @comision_teatro: Take the seat but keep the theater — use committee documents as ammunition for public fights, not quiet fixes.
- @comision_rechazar: Decline it. The caucus is small; its people belong in the streets, not drowning in subsections.

@comision_trabajar
choose-if: organizers >= 3
unavailable-subtitle: Serious committee work needs a serious cadre to spare — you have none idle.
on-arrival: political_capital += 5; funds += 3; sup_peasants += 2; absorcion += 6; sup_students -= 2

Your deputy becomes, within a year, the most competent person in the room, which in a committee is a form of power the PRI did not intend to hand over: the amendments that survive are increasingly yours, the buried report is un-buried, a budget line for rural schools exists that would not otherwise. It is real, it is unglamorous, and it is digestive — the compañero now speaks fluent subsection and dreams in fiscal years, and the antechambers count another guest settling in for the long meal.

- @post_event: Continuar.

@comision_teatro
on-arrival: sup_students += 2; legitimidad_regimen -= 2; pri_reformist_rel -= 2; expediente += 2; fe_voto += 1

You take the seat and refuse its etiquette: every document the committee generates that embarrasses the regime finds its way, at exactly the wrong moment for Bucareli, into the hands of the press and the plaza. It makes you a bad committee member and a good opposition — the PRI learns not to minute anything sensitive while you are in the room, which is its own small victory. You have kept the teeth visible; you have also spent the goodwill that would have let you actually move the budget line. The road forces the choice; you chose the street.

- @post_event: Continuar.

@comision_rechazar
on-arrival: absorcion -= 5; sup_students += 2; unity += 1; pri_reformist_rel -= 3; political_capital -= 2

You decline, on the theory the founders would recognize: that a revolutionary party's cadres belong where the people are, not entombed in the fiscal subsections of a state you mean to replace. It keeps the caucus lean and pointed outward, unabsorbed, plainly still an opposition. It also leaves the committee to the PRI and the PAN, who write the budget without you and are, quietly, relieved. Purity has a price and it is paid in millimeters not moved.

- @post_event: Continuar.

@oposicion_responsable
title: Oposición responsable
new-page: true
subtitle: The praise that poisons
face-image: img/excelsior.jpg
tags: event
view-if: via = "institucional" and pri_reformist_rel >= 32 and absorcion >= 20 and time >= respons_last + 22
priority: 2
frequency: 55
max-visits: 3
on-arrival: respons_last = time

= Oposición responsable

The editorial appears in one of the serious papers, and it is worse than any attack: it is praise. The Party's parliamentary conduct, the columnist writes, exemplifies *una oposición responsable y madura* — constructive, institutional, a credit to the democratic opening. It is meant kindly. It is quoted approvingly in the President's circle. And it lands in the assemblies like a diagnosis, because the base has spent fifty years learning exactly what the regime means when it calls a leftist *responsible*: it means housebroken.

The leadership feels the trap close from both sides. Reject the praise and you look ungrateful, unserious, incapable of taking yes for an answer. Accept it and you ratify the frame — that the good left is the quiet one, that maturity means the muzzle. The compliment is a leash offered as a bouquet.

- @responsable_rechazar: Repudiate it, sharply — from the tribune, reject the regime's certificate of good conduct. You are not responsible to it.
- @responsable_ignorar: Ignore it. A press compliment is not a policy; refuse to let a columnist set the Party's self-image.
- @responsable_aceptar: Wear it. Respectability is an asset with the middle class the left has never held; bank the legitimacy.

@responsable_rechazar
on-arrival: sup_students += 3; sup_workers += 2; absorcion -= 8; pri_reformist_rel -= 5; legitimidad_regimen -= 1; unity += 2

You use your own recognized tribune to reject the recognition: the Party is not responsible *to* the regime, you say, but to the people the regime disappears, and if maturity means silence then the Party is proudly, permanently adolescent. It is good theater and truer than theater, and it snaps the leash before it tightens — the base exhales, the columnist writes a wounded follow-up, and the antechambers file you back under *difícil.* You gave up the compliment to keep the constituency. On this road, that is the trade that keeps you yourself.

- @post_event: Continuar.

@responsable_ignorar
on-arrival: absorcion += 2; unity += 1; political_capital += 1

The leadership decides a newspaper adjective is beneath a response and moves on, which is defensible and also, quietly, a small surrender: the frame goes unchallenged, the word *responsable* attaches itself another degree, and the drift resumes at its patient rate. Not every hook must be taken; but the ones left in the water are still, slowly, reeling.

- @post_event: Continuar.

@responsable_aceptar
on-arrival: sup_middle += 4; funds += 2; absorcion += 8; pri_reformist_rel += 4; sup_students -= 3; fe_voto -= 1

You decide respectability is a resource the left has never been able to afford and cannot start refusing now: the middle class that has always feared you is, for the first time, reading that you are safe, and safe is what lets a frightened notary vote left. The support arrives, measurable, from a quarter the Party never reached. So does the cost, unmeasured until later: each degree of respectable is a degree of digested, and the young who wanted a party the regime *hated* read the editorial too, and draw their own conclusion about where the fight went.

- @post_event: Continuar.

@la_gestoria
title: La gestoría
new-page: true
subtitle: Co-opted by usefulness
face-image: img/cards/colonia.jpg
tags: event
view-if: via = "institucional" and izq_seats >= 1 and (sup_colonos >= 12 or sup_peasants >= 15) and time >= gestoria_last + 24
priority: 2
frequency: 50
max-visits: 3
on-arrival: gestoria_last = time

= La gestoría

It begins as a compliment and becomes a swamp. Because you now hold seats, the people start bringing you their problems the way they have always brought them to the PRI: not the revolution, but the water main, the missing pension, the son picked up by the judiciales, the clinic that needs a doctor. Your deputies' offices fill with the Republic's daily wounds, and every one of them is real, and every one of them can, with a phone call to the right desk, sometimes actually be fixed.

This is *gestoría* — the errand-running that is the true currency of Mexican politics, the way the PRI has bought loyalty one solved problem at a time for fifty years. Do it well and you become beloved, indispensable, re-elected. Do it well and you become, in function, exactly what you set out to destroy: a more honest window at the same office of favors.

- @gestoria_abrazar: Solve the problems. A left that fixes the water main earns a loyalty the manifesto never will.
- @gestoria_organizar: Turn petitioners into organizers — don't fix the water main, help the colonia force the city to fix it, together.
- @gestoria_rechazar: Refuse the role. You are legislators, not the PRI's honest competitors in the favor trade.

@gestoria_abrazar
on-arrival: sup_colonos += 4; sup_peasants += 3; funds -= 1; absorcion += 7; fe_voto += 2; fac_nueva_izquierda -= 2

The offices become clinics of the possible: pensions unstuck, sons retrieved, a water main that actually arrives with your name spoken over it in the colonia for a generation. The loyalty is real and it is deep and it re-elects you, and it is built on precisely the foundation the PRI built its own on — the grateful dependent, the fixed problem, the patron with a kinder face. You are winning the people. You are winning them the regime's way, and the regime, watching, is not displeased to see the left learn its trade.

- @post_event: Continuar.

@gestoria_organizar
choose-if: organizers >= 2
unavailable-subtitle: Turning petitioners into an organized bloc takes cadres to do the teaching — you are short.
on-arrival: sup_colonos += 3; sup_peasants += 2; absorcion -= 4; political_capital += 2; huelgas += 1; unity += 1

You refuse to be the window and build the crowd instead: the woman who came for a favor leaves in a comité, the water main won not by your phone call but by two hundred neighbors at the delegación who now know they can do it again without you. It is slower, it wins fewer individual cases, and it makes something the favor trade never does — colonos who are no longer petitioners but a bloc, harder to co-opt because they no longer need a patron. The reformist road, briefly, remembering it was supposed to be a *left.*

- @post_event: Continuar.

@gestoria_rechazar
on-arrival: sup_colonos -= 3; absorcion -= 3; unity += 1; pri_reformist_rel -= 1

The caucus draws a line: we legislate, we do not run errands, we are not auditioning to be a cleaner PRI. It is ideologically tidy and politically expensive — the people who came for help go where help is given, which is back to the ruling party's window, and they remember who turned them away. Purity again, and again its price: the colonia concludes the left is for speeches and the PRI is for water, and acts on the conclusion at the only poll that counts.

- @post_event: Continuar.

@la_comida
title: La comida
new-page: true
subtitle: Managed over a long lunch
face-image: img/cards/fuente_bucareli.jpg
tags: event
view-if: via = "institucional" and pri_reformist_rel >= 35 and time >= comida_last + 26 and year >= 1979
priority: 2
frequency: 45
max-visits: 3
